WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.704 --> 00:00:16.906
For many years, Hook and his pirates had searched for the hidden entrance to the Lost Boys' home,

2
00:00:18.047 --> 00:00:19.247
but had never found it.

3
00:00:20.368 --> 00:00:25.030
As the pirates followed the boys, hoping to be led to the entrance, they saw Tootles.

4
00:00:26.471 --> 00:00:32.918
As always, Tootles was way behind the other boys, who had already disappeared into their hiding place.

5
00:00:34.319 --> 00:00:37.340
The pirates were about to shoot him dead when Hook stopped them.

6
00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:44.124
"If you fire your pistols now," he roared, "the Indians will find us.

7
00:00:45.005 --> 00:00:46.966
Do you want to lose your hair?"

8
00:00:47.926 --> 00:00:53.550
Meanwhile, Tootles had disappeared, and the pirates began to run back to their ship in fear of the

9
00:00:53.610 --> 00:01:00.673
Indians. Alone with Smee, who had stayed behind, Hook calmed down and told his sad tale.

10
00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:05.075
"I want to catch all six boys at one time.

11
00:01:06.335 --> 00:01:09.477
But most of all I want their captain, Peter Pan.

12
00:01:10.977 --> 00:01:13.418
It was Peter Pan who cut off my hand."

13
00:01:14.259 --> 00:01:15.839
He shook his hook threateningly.

14
00:01:15.859 --> 00:01:19.741
"I've waited a long time to catch him with this."

15
00:01:20.981 --> 00:01:26.964
"I've heard you say many times," said Smee, "that one hook is worth a dozen hands."

16
00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:30.902
"Nonetheless, I want Peter.

17
00:01:31.563 --> 00:01:34.905
He flung my hand to a crocodile that was passing by.

18
00:01:36.266 --> 00:01:41.170
And the crocodile liked my hand so much that it has followed me ever since.

19
00:01:42.591 --> 00:01:46.995
On land and sea, it licks its lips, hoping for the rest of me.

20
00:01:47.515 --> 00:01:48.576
I can never relax."

21
00:01:50.238 --> 00:01:54.061
"In a way that's a compliment to you, Captain," said the loyal Smee.

22
00:01:54.081 --> 00:01:59.164
"It's Peter who gave the crocodile its taste for me," said Hook.

23
00:02:00.244 --> 00:02:07.766
"Luckily, that crocodile also swallowed a clock, so I always know by its ticking sound whenever it comes

24
00:02:07.867 --> 00:02:13.268
near. Without that warning, it would already have had me for supper."

25
00:02:14.548 --> 00:02:19.650
"Someday that clock will break down," said Smee, "and you'll be in big trouble."

26
00:02:19.670 --> 00:02:22.510
"Yes, that's my fear."

27
00:02:23.211 --> 00:02:26.972
Shuddering, Hook sat down on a giant mushroom for a moment.

28
00:02:27.872 --> 00:02:29.281
Suddenly he jumped up.

29
00:02:29.301 --> 00:02:30.722
"This seat is hot!"

30
00:02:32.123 --> 00:02:34.365
Hook and Smee examined the giant mushroom.

31
00:02:35.246 --> 00:02:39.229
When Smee tried to pull it out of the ground, he found it had no roots.

32
00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:42.732
Furthermore, it had smoke coming out of it.

33
00:02:43.692 --> 00:02:47.496
They had discovered the chimney of the Lost Boys' underground home.

34
00:02:48.596 --> 00:02:50.498
Now they could hear the boys' voices.

35
00:02:52.079 --> 00:02:56.203
Smee whispered, "Did you hear them say Peter Pan will be back soon?"

36
00:02:56.223 --> 00:02:58.565
"Good!" said Hook.

37
00:02:59.145 --> 00:03:02.687
"Let's return to the ship and think of a way to capture him."

38
00:03:03.728 --> 00:03:05.989
But before they left, they heard one more thing.

39
00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:11.093
Tick-tock, tick-tock, tick-tock.

40
00:03:12.494 --> 00:03:15.236
Hook gasped, "It's the crocodile!"

41
00:03:15.876 --> 00:03:16.997
and he ran away.

42
00:03:18.238 --> 00:03:19.558
Smee quickly followed.

43
00:03:20.739 --> 00:03:25.602
The boys had a clever way in and out of their underground home, and they used it to

44
00:03:25.642 --> 00:03:26.023
come out.

45
00:03:28.044 --> 00:03:31.806
Tootles, who had been hiding from the pirates in the woods, joined the rest of his friends.

46
00:03:33.127 --> 00:03:34.327
He was very excited.

47
00:03:34.347 --> 00:03:37.429
"I saw a wonderful thing in the sky!

48
00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:40.090
A great white bird!

49
00:03:40.431 --> 00:03:41.811
It's flying this way."

50
00:03:41.831 --> 00:03:45.093
"What kind of bird?"

51
00:03:45.673 --> 00:03:46.374
the others asked.

52
00:03:46.394 --> 00:03:52.437
"I don't know," replied Tootles, "but it looks almost like a girl.

53
00:03:54.158 --> 00:03:59.312
It flies as though it's in pain, and it keeps crying 'Poor Wendy'."

54
00:04:03.093 --> 00:04:05.334
remember now," said Slightly.

55
00:04:05.354 --> 00:04:08.715
"I think there are birds called the Wendy Bird."

56
00:04:10.055 --> 00:04:10.956
"Here it comes!"

57
00:04:11.676 --> 00:04:13.636
shouted Curly, pointing upward.

58
00:04:14.656 --> 00:04:18.257
They could hear Wendy's cries—along with the tinkle of Tinker Bell.

59
00:04:20.058 --> 00:04:23.959
With Peter far away, Tinker Bell didn't have to act nice anymore.

60
00:04:24.859 --> 00:04:25.900
She could do what she wanted.

61
00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:31.051
In the air, the jealous fairy had been pinching Wendy all over her body.

62
00:04:32.392 --> 00:04:34.213
Seeing the boys, she stopped.

63
00:04:34.233 --> 00:04:36.335
"Hello, Tink!"

64
00:04:36.975 --> 00:04:37.696
yelled the boys.

65
00:04:39.177 --> 00:04:41.059
Tinker Bell landed in a nearby tree.

66
00:04:41.079 --> 00:04:43.060
"Hello, boys.

67
00:04:43.521 --> 00:04:47.404
Peter wants you to shoot the Wendy Bird," she lied.

68
00:04:48.445 --> 00:04:53.269
Never one to question Peter's wishes, Tootles immediately aimed his bow and arrow.

69
00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:57.212
The others watched Wendy, who was still up in the sky.

70
00:04:58.604 --> 00:05:00.626
"Peter will be so proud of you!"

71
00:05:01.206 --> 00:05:02.907
Tinker Bell said encouragingly.

72
00:05:03.968 --> 00:05:08.972
Tootles fired, and Wendy fluttered to the ground, an arrow in her chest.
